      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/brogan_oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Dennis M. Brogan founded the Willow River Land and Irrigation Company to build dams and canals for local crops and orchards.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/brogan_oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Brogan sits in the valley of Willow Creek, a southeast-flowing tributary of the Malheur River in eastern Oregon.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brogan%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town is located at the north end of a now-abandoned Union Pacific Railroad branch line from Vale.",
